# C31 remediation after attempt-03 (8/8/8/8/8, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 persisted issuance link reused after relaunch | `Rotation.issued_by` is session-only (`#[serde(skip)]`): operation IDs restart with the core, so a relaunch never restores the link and the rotation resumes with nothing to reveal. The link is also exact: a rotation's key is held, offered or forgotten only through the result that is the Runtime key Version of its old key (`ChangeRecord::is_issuance_of`, `issuance_held`, `forget_issuance`); any other result, including a Gateway rotation or another application's issuance with the same ID, is untouched. Test: `ui_v2_reviews::a_reused_operation_id_after_relaunch_never_links_another_key` (the link is absent from the saved state; after a relaunch an issuance for another application provably reuses the former ID; the old rotation stays Resumed with no Reveal; acknowledging it leaves the new key held; the new key is revealable from its own result) | `features.rs`, `change_domain.rs`, `rotation_domain.rs`, `authority.rs` |
| R2 failed second issuance hidden | A rejected or not-sent key change of a rotation is shown as an alert with the core's sanitized result, apart from the rotation it leaves unchanged ("No new key was issued…", or for a removal "The old key was not removed…"), with an explicit "Review again…" that opens a new review; nothing is sent by itself. The sheet re-renders when it marks the previous change's results as seen. Test: "shows a failed second issuance apart from the rotation it leaves unchanged" | `review-sheet.tsx` |
| R3 topic verdicts without icons | Every topic verdict in the Playground carries an icon with its words, in both directions: blocked (ShieldX), monitor only (Eye), unnamed match (AlertTriangle), not detected (CheckCircle2), not reported (CircleHelp). Test: "gives every topic verdict an icon and words, for the prompt and the response, in the production Playground" | `runtime-view.tsx` |

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
# C31 remediation after attempt-02 (8/7/8/8/7, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 in-flight rotation lost on context retirement | A Runtime key Version or Delete records the tenant it was made in (`ChangeRecord.rotation_tenant`). When its context retires before it settles (tenant switch, credential replacement), the record is detached like a Gateway change and its settlement still drives that tenant's rotation, with the one-time key and reply dropped (only the read-back key, never its secret, is kept for the rotation). The other tenant sees nothing; returning shows the issuance or removal as established or unconfirmed, reconcilable by a read, and nothing is resent. Tests: `ui_v2_reviews::a_switch_during_issuance_keeps_the_rotation_with_its_tenant`, `a_switch_during_removal_keeps_the_outcome_with_its_tenant` | `change_domain.rs` |
| R2 rotation facts lost on a failed save | Facts the service established (issuance, removal, reconciliation) are saved by `keep_rotation_fact`: a failure keeps them in memory (never rolled back), reports `RotationView.unsaved` (shown as an alert in the rotation panel), and every publication retries the save (`retry_rotation_save` at the start of `sync_changes`; any successful save also clears it). Nothing remote is replayed. An intent's own save keeps its refusal semantics; acknowledging forgets the held key only after the acknowledgement is saved. Test: `rotation_facts_survive_a_storage_failure_and_are_saved_on_recovery` (issuance and removal under `fail_saves`, refused acknowledgement keeps the key, recovery, relaunch shows the original timestamps, one POST and one DELETE) | `rotation_domain.rs`, `authority.rs`, `rotation-panel.tsx` |
| R3 removal opened on a refused acknowledgement | "Application updated" opens the old key's removal only once the snapshot shows the recorded acknowledgement; a refusal or failed delivery shows an alert and changes nothing; an unconfirmed delivery says so and waits for the observation. Test: "opens the old key's removal only once the acknowledgement is recorded" (deniedStore, invalidInput, staleContext, lost delivery, then the recorded acknowledgement opens it once) | `review-sheet.tsx` |
| R4 Harness proposal not routed into the v2 sheet | The v2 Administration watches for a proposal in review whose native review is open, opens the product and tab of its kind and shows the review sheet with the exact draft under that review; the embedded inventory no longer handles it. Typed confirmation still gates Apply and leaving discards the review. Test: "opens a Harness proposal's native review in the review sheet" | `administration.tsx`, `administration-view.tsx` |
| R5 applied panel without its receipt | `ChangeResultView.settledAt` is the core's clock when the settlement and readback were recorded (stable across observations). A live or removed result shows Tenant, Resource, Name, Revision (not for a removal) and "Read back at", each "Not reported" when the service did not return it; unconfirmed or failed results never show it. Test: "names what a confirmed change established" | `change_domain.rs`, `review-sheet.tsx`, `client.ts` |
| Optional | The embedded inventory's lead says changes open a review and apply only after confirmation | `administration-view.tsx` |

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
# C31 remediation after attempt-01 (7/6/6/6/6, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 secret lifetime | The core binds disclosure to the review: each applied change records the review it came from, and `DiscardChange` on an applied review forgets every one-time key its changes returned, settled or not; a forget on an unsettled change marks it so the key is dropped the moment it lands (`forget_on_settle`), never held. The review sheet ends every review it opened on each exit: Done, Escape, the scrim, Finish later, and unmount (navigation, tenant switch, window close), the last deferred one tick so a development re-mount cancels it. Tests: `ui_v2_reviews::a_key_that_lands_after_the_review_closed_is_dropped_on_arrival` (delayed issuance, review left while the write is on the wire, result `forgotten`, rotation `resumed`, Reveal refused, nothing shown), `leaving_an_applied_review_retires_its_held_key`, and `administration.test.tsx` "a review exit ends the review in the core, also before its change settles and on unmount" | `change_domain.rs`, `review-sheet.tsx` |
| R2 reconciliation evidence | An unconfirmed issuance keeps the key name its review named (`Rotation.pending_name`); only a key of that application with that exact name, and not the old key, confirms it. Absence is established only by the whole inventory in one read (a first page that is also the last), or by a key detail read, which walks the whole inventory (its `absent` is authoritative). Tests: `a_failed_or_unknown_issuance_claims_nothing_until_a_key_is_read_back` (an unrelated key of the application leaves it unconfirmed), `a_rejected_or_unknown_removal_keeps_the_reminder_until_the_key_is_read_back_gone` (a non-first final page without the old key completes nothing), `a_key_detail_walk_reconciles_an_unconfirmed_removal` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `management_domain.rs` |
| R3 issuedBy vs validator | Acknowledging the deployment forgets the held key (the operator states the application has it); `issuedBy` is emitted only while the key is held and the stage may reveal it (`issued`, `issuanceUnconfirmed`), and the TypeScript validator admits exactly those stages. Test: `acknowledging_the_deployment_forgets_the_held_key` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `client.ts` |
| R4 completed Version without a found readback | Any sent Version (completed or unknown) whose readback did not find the key is an explicit `issuanceUnconfirmed` rotation with the held key still revealable once and a reconciliation path (the reviewed name); nothing is reissued. A refused Version shows the core's result as an alert. Test: `a_completed_version_whose_readback_missed_is_an_unconfirmed_issuance` | `rotation_domain.rs`, `review-sheet.tsx`, `rotation-panel.tsx` |
| R5 applied success not action-specific | `appliedState`: a delete is removed only when completed without failure and read back absent; any other action is live only when completed without failure and read back found; unknown or completed-with-failure is unconfirmed; anything else failed. Reconciliation reads the reviewed item itself (its detail by ID, or the inventory by name for a creation; Gateway kinds through the workspace's Gateway read) and shows what that read established. Toasts confirm completions for the tenant they belong to | `review-sheet.tsx` (tests in `administration.test.tsx`) |
| R6 per-tab contracts, Gateway review, inventory-driven actions | Red Team tabs render their own read surface (Overview tiles and window, Targets, Scans, Attack results, Reports); model tabs render Overview, Model scans or Skill scans. Gateway changes open the shell's review sheet with typed confirmation and secret disposal, keeping the draft hook and note; Gateway create, row and workspace actions and labels come from the inventory. Runtime create and row actions are exactly the tab's admitted actions in the inventory's order | `red-team-view.tsx`, `gateway-view.tsx`, `administration-view.tsx`, `administration.tsx` |
